{
 "version": 1,
 "notes": [
  "Keys are ASCII and lowercase only: Windows-mounted drives are case-insensitive, so uppercase letters use a cap_ prefix.",
  "tier 1 = appears in sampling.pdf; tier 2 = extras you will likely need. n = number of samples to write.",
  "kind: normal | tall (stretched vertically, write large) | display (big operators, write large) | accent (written above a letter; the cutter records the offset)",
  "font_map: (PDF font family without size, character) -> symbol key. Missing pairs should render a visible placeholder box.",
  "font_map extras: stretch=vertical -> stretched to ink box measured from the PDF raster; pad = horizontal search margin in pt (default 0.6); role = bracket piece merging.",
  "font_map anchor=topright: sample's top-right ink corner is pinned to the top-right of the measured box and scaled uniformly (used for the radical sign).",
  "batch: field on a symbol; make_sheet.py --batch NAME selects them. role=overlay: zero-width glyph (\\not slash) centered on the glyph it crosses.",
  "font_map ink_em=[top,bottom]: glyph ink box = advance width x (top*size above origin .. bottom*size below), sample stretched to it. anchor=fitw: sample width fitted to the glyph advance (arrows). COMPOSITES in extract_items.py merge overlapping glyph pairs (=+arrowhead etc.)."
 ],
